course: dictionary
lesson: 15958
title: Untested
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word untested is made of three parts: un- means not, test means try or check, and -ed shows it describes something. So untested means not yet tried, checked or proved to work. «The new bridge is untested, so nobody should drive on it yet.» The clue is nobody should drive on it yet: it has not been checked.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The new bridge is not yet tried, so nobody should drive on it yet» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: You can also use untested for a person. «The untested goalkeeper was nervous before the big final.» The goalkeeper has not yet shown what they can do in a hard game, so the words around it tell you the meaning.
explain: Untested is used in many subjects. In science an untested idea is only a hypothesis until an experiment tests it. In medicine and safety, untested products can be dangerous, so they must be checked first.
fact: Untested means not yet tried, checked or proved to work.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so untested is the opposite of tested.
fact: «An untested medicine can be dangerous, so doctors test it first.»
fact: In science, an untested idea is only a hypothesis until an experiment tests it.
fact: In sport and stories, an untested player or hero has not yet shown what they can do in a hard situation.
exercise: «The rocket design is still untested, so the engineers will run more trials.» What does untested mean here? | Painted bright red | Very fast | *Not yet tried or checked | Finished and proved to work
exercise: Mia says the new game code is untested. What does that suggest? | It has been checked many times and works perfectly | *It has not been checked yet, so it may have bugs | It is a kind of computer | It is made for very young children
exercise: «The untested goalkeeper was nervous before the big final.» What does untested tell us about the goalkeeper? | Has won every game this season | *Has not yet shown what they can do in a hard game | Is the team captain | Is very old
test: «The untested medicine stayed in the lab until doctors had tested it.» What does untested mean? | Tested and found safe | Expensive | *Not yet tried or checked | Sold in every shop
test: In science, an untested idea is only a what, until an experiment tests it? | *Hypothesis | Result | Fact | Law
exam: What does the prefix un- in untested mean? | Again | Very | *Not | Before
